{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 65, :comments ["<b>Save Caleb son of Jephunneh.</b> He placed Caleb before Joshua, for so the Holy One, blessed be He, always places him before Joshua, because he preceded Joshua in his zeal for the Holy One, blessed be He, in the matter of the spies — as it is written (Numbers 13:30): ״ויהס כלב את העם״, and further because He called him (ibid. 14) ״My servant.״ But Moses always places Joshua before Caleb, and this is on account of the rank of wisdom. And as for what it says, ״and there was not left of them a man״ (ולא נותר מהם איש) — our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ״a man״ (איש) and not a woman; from here it follows that the women were not included in the decree of the wilderness. And upon this basis the section of the daughters of Zelophehad was juxtaposed to the numbering of Israel, in keeping with what they said in the Midrash: the men were haters of the Land and said, ״Let us appoint a head and return to Egypt,״ but the women cherished the Land and said, ״Give us an inheritance״; therefore the section of the daughters of Zelophehad was juxtaposed here."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:23.106237343Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}